 Objective 

• Build an inorder-threaded BST from user input, where null links are replaced by threads to 
  the inorder successor/predecessor. 
• Accept several nodes from the user in one run and find the successor of each one using the threads, 
  with no recursion or stack. 
• Identify how each successor is reached: via a right thread, or via a child link (the leftmost node 
  of the right subtree). 
• Handle the edge cases: the last node has no successor, and a value that is not in the tree is reported as not found.
